cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Audit-Vorbereitung
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as part of the SimpleAct AI Governance Framework."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: SimpleAct-Compliance
repository-code: "https://github.com/SimpleAct-Compliance/simpleact-ai-audit-readiness"
license: MIT
abstract: "The difference between a state an organisation has reached and one it can show, under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 and the GDPR. Covers the three properties an audit actually tests — attributability, traceability and producibility — the nine-section evidence pack in the order an audit works through it, the four audit trails that require nothing to be overwritten, the four kinds of gap and why provider-side gaps belong with procurement rather than the remediation list, and an honest account of what a readiness score cannot measure: it can only compute over the systems already in the register."
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - GDPR
  - audit readiness
  - evidence pack
  - traceability
  - gap remediation
  - Article 14
  - Article 25
  - AI governance
  - SimpleAct
